nd it won’t light because the inside is full of pure fuel with no air — just dangerous vapor above the liquid if it’s leaking. The pipe is that sealed can, continuously replenished. I’m not trying to be argumentative — I sincerely respect the instinct you’re describing, because it’s right in many other contexts. Does this distinction between open-air fuel paths and sealed, pressurized, oxygen-free pipes make sense?
